<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amshuvarman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 605–621</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amshuvarman was a ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/licchavi">Licchavi</a> period, first a powerful minister under King Shivadeva I and then holder of royal titles. His inscriptions show a well-organised administration, and he built the Kailashakuta palace in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathmandu-valley">Kathmandu Valley</a>. Tibetan tradition makes him the father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhrikuti">Bhrikuti</a>, the Nepalese wife of the Tibetan king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songtsen-gampo">Songtsen Gampo</a>.</p></div>
